-- ============================================================================
-- DC31 - Basin & Charge EXPERT (advanced tier) goes deep.
--
-- Flips (basin, advanced) onto the DC1 deep path by inserting its ACTIVE
-- academy_course_structures row, generated from the repo manifest
-- src/content/courses/basin/advanced/manifest.json (emitted by a generator,
-- not hand-typed), and seeding the six module quiz banks plus the final exam.
-- Answer keys live only here and in the table.
--
-- Six modules, 27 lessons: the reference basin, the forward march, the erosion
-- event, generation and expulsion, what the model buys, and the charge
-- workflow. LAST TIER OF THE GEOSCIENCE LADDER: with it basin completes at all
-- three tiers and all ten geoscience apps are fully deep.
--
-- Every numeric item traces to the basin teaching oracle in
-- src/lib/basinTeaching.js over the @petrolord/engines forward model
-- (SimulationEngine on the golden reference basin), and reproduces the live
-- NG11 Expert capstone answer key: final_ro 1.6718288798752388, final_temp
-- 149.76037539670858, final_tr 0.7423743797385286, generated
-- 13946.54641524398, expelled 10048.985378825158, ro_delta
-- 0.05665081052235643. chargeLab.test.js pins the panel math to those values.
--
-- Tier positioning: the tiers below own burial, heat and the kinetics; this
-- tier owns the composition. The potential is closed-form (2720 x
-- 345.33834344581027 x 0.04 x 0.5 = 18786.405883452077 kg/m2) and generated
-- mass is exactly potential x TR. The erosion event is a phantom shale layer
-- (600 m deposited at 20 Ma, removed at 10 Ma) whose hot decade peaks at
-- 168.51433459340572 C at 18 Ma; the thermometer forgets it (present-day
-- temperatures differ 1e-4 C between runs) while the reflectance ratchet
-- remembers (delta Ro 57x its tolerance). THE SQUEEZE: final expelled mass is
-- an exact float64 identity, gen(11 Ma) 13907.011498614682 minus the
-- phantom-decade cap 3858.026119789524, set at 11 Ma and held by the monotone
-- expulsion rule through the rebound; 764.78 of the event's 1258.65 kg/m2
-- charge contribution is cap squeeze, not extra generation. Signature grows
-- convexly with amount (0.0144 / 0.0567 / 0.1529 at 300 / 600 / 900 m).
--
-- Bank standard: measured on the length RANK of the correct option and checked
-- for cyclic key sequences, answer-index skew, within-pool near-duplicates and
-- same-claim option pairs before seeding. Across the 132 questions the correct
-- option is longest in 7 pct and shortest in 5 pct.
--
-- Enrollment grandfathering: enforced_from defaults to now() on first insert;
-- the ON CONFLICT update deliberately leaves enforced_from unchanged.
--
-- Ladder note: an ADVANCED enrollment needs an unrevoked PROFESSIONAL
-- certification on the SAME app, so the dry-run probes back-stop a basin
-- professional cert in-transaction, and P3b checks prove the basin Associate
-- AND Professional tiers are left undisturbed at 132 questions each.
--
-- New bs-charge-explorer panel. NO DDL. Data only.
-- ============================================================================

values ('basin', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-the-reference-basin","title":"The Reference Basin","lesson_keys":["l01-what-this-tier-adds","l02-four-layers-and-a-history","l03-the-heat-flow-history","l04-the-basin-panel-map"]},{"key":"m02-the-forward-march","title":"The Forward March","lesson_keys":["l01-time-steps-and-instant-deposition","l02-geometry-every-step","l03-transient-heat","l04-the-layer-centre-convention","l05-elastic-rebound"]},{"key":"m03-the-erosion-event","title":"The Erosion Event","lesson_keys":["l01-the-phantom-layer","l02-the-hot-decade","l03-the-thermometer-forgets","l04-the-signature-is-two-runs","l05-amount-sensitivity"]},{"key":"m04-generation-and-expulsion","title":"Generation and Expulsion","lesson_keys":["l01-potential-mass","l02-generated-is-potential-times-tr","l03-the-saturation-bucket","l04-the-squeeze","l05-expulsion-is-monotone"]},{"key":"m05-what-the-model-buys","title":"What the Model Buys","lesson_keys":["l01-the-charge-statement","l02-what-a-steady-model-would-miss","l03-limits-of-the-model","l04-sanity-checks"]},{"key":"m06-the-charge-workflow","title":"The Charge Workflow","lesson_keys":["l01-the-workflow-end-to-end","l02-quality-control","l03-the-capstone-walkthrough","l04-the-ladder-closes"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
on conflict (app_slug, tier) do update
  set structure = excluded.structure,
      content_version = excluded.content_version,
      active = true,
